<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buyruk Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1206</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buyruk Khan was a son of the Naiman ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inanch-bilge-khan">Inanch Bilge Khan</a>, who after his father's death in the 1190s ruled part of the Naiman khanate in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altai-mountains">Altai</a> mountains while his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tayang-khan">Tayang Khan</a> ruled the rest. The brothers' rivalry weakened the Naiman against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Temüjin</a>, the future Genghis Khan, and Buyruk was killed by Mongol forces in 1206.</p></div>
